title: The storage boundary
tags: Storage
kind: reference
audience: dev
summary: The traits everything above the store speaks — Rows, Log, WriteTxn, Begin, Database — the lookups built on them, and the contract test a backend must pass.

`crates/daemon/src/store.rs` holds the traits every module above the store speaks:
the event log, revert, the watcher, reconcile, the schema, duplicates, orphans,
mounts, the query source. `kvstore/` is the one implementation.

|!Trait |!What |
|`Rows` |the data model's primary state: a metarecord's existence and version, its rows (all, or by name), in no particular order; insert a row, delete the row holding a value under a name; create and delete a metarecord; the forest's positions; and, off the indexes with no record read, the ids holding a field (`holder_ids`) or a value (`value_holder_ids`: its posting, `Nothing`'s `absent` set) |
|`Log` |writes, operations and their snapshots, one operation by id, the bounded backward reads, HEAD and the first operation, labels, the range deletions of pruning and retention |
|`WriteTxn` |one write transaction: one `log::Writer` write |
|`Begin` |opens a transaction; also `check`, `reindex`, `backup_to`, and the interrupter a task's Stop uses |
|`Database` |all of it: what a loaded repository holds (`store::Handle`) |

''A row has no id'' in these traits: it is its metarecord's, its name and its value
([[No duplicate rows]]), and a row is inserted, or deleted, by those. What the store
keeps to find a row quickly is its own business ([[Store tables]]).

The workers' repository-wide lookups — the holders of a value, the owners of a string
field, the tracked files with their sizes, the hashed orphans, the stored hashes of
some files — are `crate::lookup`, built on `value_holder_ids` and `holder_ids`: the
records that answer come from the indexes, and only they are read. The schema check's
candidate questions (`wrong_type`, `count_over`, `count_under`, `missing`,
`typed_missing`) are the key-value store's own, read off its counters and postings.

There used to be a `Questions` trait here, each question with a default derived from
`Rows` alone by reading every row of a field, or every record — correct on any
backend, written when SQLite was one. The key-value store overrode only the schema
check's, and not in a write transaction: a few tags added under a schema on `tag`
read 2.2 million keys (November 2026). The defaults are gone with SQLite's reason
for them.

`tests/store_contract.rs` asks every method through the traits only — the file a
second backend would have to pass — and holds the schema check's questions to a
derivation from every record's rows.
